WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:09.208
It was raining the next time Aunt Polly attended a Ladies' Aid meeting.

2
00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:16.331
When she came home, her face was flushed, and her hair was damp and windblown.

3
00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:23.773
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you look lovely! I didn't know your hair curled in the rain."

4
00:00:23.774 --> 00:00:27.073
Aunt Polly tried to smooth her hair.

5
00:00:27.074 --> 00:00:30.868
"No, don't do that!" Pollyanna cried.

6
00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:35.085
But Aunt Polly had another topic to discuss besides hair.

7
00:00:35.086 --> 00:00:40.399
"Why did you go to the Ladies' Aid meeting to talk about that little beggar boy?

8
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.470
I was so embarrassed when they told me this afternoon!"

9
00:00:44.471 --> 00:00:51.712
"I didn't know the ladies would be more concerned with orphans overseas than Jimmy," Pollyanna burst out.

10
00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:53.967
"Or I would have stayed home.

11
00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:57.978
But I've written to my Ladies' Aid out West about taking him.

12
00:00:57.979 --> 00:01:01.644
So now we'll just have to wait and see what happens."

13
00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:04.329
She paused for a breath.

14
00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:13.306
"Oh, please may I fix your hair like I did Mrs. Snow's? You'd look so pretty!"

15
00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:19.110
"Pollyanna!" Aunt Polly scolded, but she was secretly pleased.

16
00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:23.478
It had been a long time since anyone had told her that she was pretty.

17
00:01:23.479 --> 00:01:32.774
"You didn't say I couldn't do it!" Pollyanna cried as she ran for the stairs. "Let's go upstairs."

18
00:01:32.775 --> 00:01:38.073
"But, Pollyanna, the Ladies' Aid . . ."

19
00:01:38.074 --> 00:01:44.926
Aunt Polly had that helpless feeling again as she trailed upstairs after her niece.

20
00:01:44.927 --> 00:01:50.159
The next thing Aunt Polly knew, she was sitting at the dressing table in her room.

21
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.687
Pollyanna began styling her hair.

22
00:01:55.688 --> 00:02:02.052
"Turn so you can't see yourself in the mirror," Pollyanna said before leaving the room.

23
00:02:02.053 --> 00:02:06.764
A moment later she returned with a handkerchief that she slipped over Aunt Polly's eyes.

24
00:02:06.765 --> 00:02:10.058
"What are you doing?" Aunt Polly cried.

25
00:02:10.059 --> 00:02:18.006
Pollyanna giggled as she pinned a lacy shawl around Aunt Polly's shoulders.

26
00:02:18.007 --> 00:02:23.428
Then she remembered the rosebush that climbed the trellis outside her bedroom window.

27
00:02:23.429 --> 00:02:28.913
Aunt Polly tried to resist as Pollyanna pulled her down the hall.

28
00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:33.263
"Where are you taking me?" Aunt Polly said.

29
00:02:33.264 --> 00:02:43.298
"You'll see." Pollyanna leaned out her window and plucked a red rose, which she tucked behind Aunt Polly's ear.

30
00:02:43.299 --> 00:02:51.269
She removed the blindfold and held up a hand mirror. "Aren't you glad I dressed you up?" Aunt

31
00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:58.764
Polly took in her surroundings and her own reflection. Then

32
00:02:58.765 --> 00:03:05.551
she gave a startled yelp and fled to her room. At

33
00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:10.264
that moment Pollyanna saw a carriage coming up the driveway. "Dr.

34
00:03:10.265 --> 00:03:16.713
Chilton!" she called with delight from the window. "Are you looking for me?" "Yes,

35
00:03:16.714 --> 00:03:20.359
will you come outside?" Rushing

36
00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:25.980
into Aunt Polly's room, Pollyanna found her flushed and angry. Aunt

37
00:03:25.981 --> 00:03:29.268
Polly was pulling the pins from the shawl. "Pollyanna,

38
00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:31.840
how could you do this to me? You

39
00:03:31.841 --> 00:03:36.927
dressed me up, and then . . ." Aunt Polly shook her head in horror. "Let

40
00:03:36.928 --> 00:03:40.565
me be seen !"

41
00:03:40.566 --> 00:03:45.102
"But you looked perfectly lovely, Aunt Polly."

42
00:03:45.103 --> 00:03:49.006
"Lovely!" Aunt Polly said scornfully.

43
00:03:49.007 --> 00:03:53.441
She flung the shawl aside and attacked her hair with shaking fingers.

44
00:03:53.442 --> 00:03:59.381
"Oh, Aunt Polly, please let your hair stay!"

45
00:03:59.382 --> 00:04:08.438
"Absolutely not!" Aunt Polly pulled her hair back so tightly that not a single curl remained.

46
00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:17.380
"But you looked so pretty!" Pollyanna was almost sobbing as she left the room.

47
00:04:17.381 --> 00:04:22.309
She went outside, where Dr. Chilton was waiting in his carriage.

48
00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:25.638
"Mr. Pendleton would like to see you now," he said.

49
00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:28.108
"Can you come with me?"

50
00:04:28.109 --> 00:04:34.996
Pollyanna was suddenly cheered up. "Let me ask Aunt Polly."

51
00:04:34.997 --> 00:04:39.133
She returned a few moments later, looking serious.

52
00:04:39.134 --> 00:04:43.840
"What's the matter?" Dr. Chilton asked as Pollyanna climbed in.

53
00:04:43.841 --> 00:04:48.888
"Aunt Polly doesn't want anything to do with me right now."

54
00:04:48.889 --> 00:04:55.763
The doctor hesitated. "Was that your aunt I saw with you at the window?"

55
00:04:55.764 --> 00:04:59.232
Pollyanna nodded and took a deep breath.

56
00:04:59.233 --> 00:05:04.885
"That's the whole trouble.

57
00:05:04.886 --> 00:05:11.932
I fixed her hair, and she looked so pretty. Didn't you think she looked lovely?"

58
00:05:11.933 --> 00:05:16.845
The doctor replied so quietly that Pollyanna could barely hear him.

59
00:05:16.846 --> 00:05:20.748
"Yes, I thought she looked lovely."

60
00:05:20.749 --> 00:05:29.059
"Oh, I'm glad!" Pollyanna looked happy again. "I'll be sure to tell her."

61
00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.796
"No!" To Pollyanna's alarm, Dr. Chilton was almost shouting.

62
00:05:33.797 --> 00:05:36.389
"Don't ever tell her that!"

63
00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.676
"Why? I'd think you'd be glad—"

64
00:05:39.677 --> 00:05:43.700
"But she might not be."

65
00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:47.617
Pollyanna considered this for a moment before nodding in agreement.

66
00:05:47.618 --> 00:05:51.810
"After all, she ran because she spotted you."

67
00:05:51.811 --> 00:05:56.914
"That's what I thought," Dr. Chilton said softly.

